message: "If you use this work or its derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "US Care Safety Signals"
abstract: >-
  Analyses of publicly available US federal data on patient and caregiver
  safety in healthcare facilities. Five modules: CMS-published
  hospital-acquired pressure injury rates (PSI-03) across 3,056 US acute care
  hospitals with Hospital-Acquired Condition Reduction Program status for
  FY2026; resident-handling injuries (5,654 cases) and violence against
  caregivers (2,291 cases) among 25,860 nursing-facility cases reported to
  OSHA's Injury Tracking Application for 2025; a graded crosswalk linking
  8,047 OSHA establishments to CMS-certified nursing homes; and an
  out-of-sample validation of both narrative classification rules against
  OSHA's OIICS coding on 28,074 nursing-facility cases from 2024. Facilities
  are identified by federal identifier and state only.
type: dataset
